# M3 — `assertUnprivilegedOnce()` deleted from withUser.
#
# V1: pg_hba is `trust` for local connections, so a one-character typo in
# APP_DATABASE_URL connects SUCCESSFULLY as whatever role it names, with no password
# error. statesman_migrator is a MEMBER of statesman_owner, and ownership bypasses RLS
# without rolsuper or rolbypassrls (V4) — so the typo'd URL yields a connection for which
# every tenancy policy is inert, and the only thing that notices is this call.
#
# It stayed green at 44/44 because the integration harness has its own role guard
# (assertTestConnectionIdentity) which IS fatal — but it runs on a psql connection, not on
# the pg pool withUser uses, so it cannot see the production guard disappear.
#
# The two named catchers are the V3 and V1 legs respectively: the migrator (privileged
# only by MEMBERSHIP, which a rolsuper/rolbypassrls predicate passes) and the cluster
# superuser. A guard that checked attributes alone would reject the second and admit the
# first, so one catcher is not enough.
id: M3
title: `await assertUnprivilegedOnce()` deleted from withUser's body
expect: caught
proves: the production role assertion (canon 6.1 step 1, V1/V3/V4) rejects BOTH an attribute-privileged and a membership-privileged role
expect-test: refuses `authenticator`, which an ATTRIBUTE-ONLY predicate would pass
expect-test: refuses the cluster superuser, naming the SUPERUSER attribute

file: tests/support/scoped-pg/scoped.ts
count: 1
